cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "dsdbench: a benchmark for detecting simulated driving trajectories"
authors:
  - name: "dsdbench contributors"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark that measures driving-simulator realism by how well machine
  learning discriminators can separate simulated trajectories from real ones.
  It pairs a deterministic C++17 kinematic-bicycle simulator (pure pursuit
  with injectable error models) with a data layer, three discriminator
  architectures, and a statistical evaluation harness (scene-clustered BCa
  bootstrap, exact permutation tests, calibration, slice analysis with FDR
  control and regression gating).
keywords:
  - simulation
  - driving
  - benchmark
  - discriminators
  - calibration
  - bootstrap
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dsdbench/driving-scenario-discriminator-bench"
